with syne alle thaire Jyfe tyme.\n\nLAWE. (1) To laugh: Nomninale MS.\n\nLWED Ignorant. Sce Laird.\n\n(2) Rough violent ; brutal. West\n\nLAWES.\n\nLenges all at laysere, and lokes one the wallys\n\nLA WESTE. The lowest. North.\n\nWhare they ware laweste the ledcs to assaille. LAWFUL-CASE. An interj. of surprize.\n\nLAWING. (1) Going t0 law. Linc.\n\nLA WGIIE.\n\nLow .\n\nHampole.\n\n(2) Lawing of cutting the balls, or thrce claws of the fore-feet. dogs; out\n\nLAWN. The same as Launde, 9\n\nLAWLESS-MAN.\n\nLAWNDER. The sliding iron in thc fore-part of a plough. Var. dial",
